<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §4 — "the sharp end". One vanilla
    NegativeFishingOutcomeDef keyed to RUT_CoolantEel.

    VANILLA GATE, re-read from source at build (not trusted from the spec):
    FishingUtility.GetNegativeFishingOutcomes rolls Rand.Chance(0.02f) — 2% per
    completed fishing job — and then refuses if
    GenTicks.TicksGame - map.waterBodyTracker.lastNegativeCatchTick <= 300000,
    i.e. a 5-day map-wide cooldown. ⚠️ The class's own named constant
    NegativeCatchCooldownTicks = 120000 (2 days) is DEAD: the executed code uses
    the literal 300000, the same value RareCatchCooldownTicks carries. The
    spec's cited "2% / 5-day" therefore matches what actually runs — via the
    literal, not via the constant that appears to name it.

    The outcome is only reachable at all when the eel is in the water body's
    CommonFish or UncommonFish list, which is what the biome fishTypes patch
    arranges. No extra gate of our own is needed or wanted.

    ElectricalBurn, not Bite: a NegativeFishingOutcomeDef carries exactly one
    damageDef, and the shock is the characteristic one. It is a vanilla
    DamageDef (ParentName Flame, armorCategory Heat, workerClass
    DamageWorker_AddInjury, its own ElectricalBurn hediff) so no addsHediff
    entry is needed — the damage def brings its own.

    Register law: ban 1. The letter says what the pawn felt and nothing about
    what the water, the walls, or the hum are doing. It does not say the eel
    did it on purpose, it does not say anything noticed, and it explains
    nothing. INVENTED: damage range 8~14 (roughly the piranha-attack band,
    6~15, for a comparable once-per-5-days event).
  -->

  <NegativeFishingOutcomeDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_NegativeFishingOutcome_CoolantEel</defName>
    <fishType>RUT_CoolantEel</fishType>
    <letterLabel>Something in the canal</letterLabel>
    <letterText>{PAWN_nameDef} had a line in the canal when the water went hard and bright, all at once, from one end of the channel to the other.\n\nThe burns run up one arm. Nothing was landed, and the surface is flat again.</letterText>
    <letterDef>NegativeEvent</letterDef>
    <damageDef>ElectricalBurn</damageDef>
    <damageAmountRange>8~14</damageAmountRange>
  </NegativeFishingOutcomeDef>

</Defs>
